        <obo:IAO_0000115>The CRF sector (IPCC 2006) &apos;fuel combustion&apos; is a sector defined by the 2006 IPCC Guidelines for National Greenhouse Gas Inventories:
Emissions from the intentional oxidation of materials within an apparatus that is designed to raise heat and provide it either as heat or as mechanical work to a process or for use away from the apparatus.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>2006 IPCC Guidelines for National Greenhouse Gas Inventories, Volume 2, Chapter 2.2, https://www.ipcc-nggip.iges.or.jp/public/2006gl/</obo:IAO_0000119>
