    <!-- https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00010374 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00010374">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00000227"/>
        <obo:BFO_0000050 rdf:resource="https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00010172"/>
        <oeo:OEO_00000504 rdf:resource="https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00000242"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The CRF sector (IPCC 2006) &apos;electrical equipment&apos; is an industry sector defined by the 2006 IPCC Guidelines for National Greenhouse Gas Inventories:
Electrical equipment is used in the transmission and distribution of electricity above 1 kV. SF6 is used in gasinsulated switchgear (GIS), gas circuit breakers (GCB), gas-insulated transformers (GIT), gas-insulated lines (GIL), outdoor gas-insulated instrument transformers, reclosers, switches, ring main units and other equipment.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>2006 IPCC Guidelines for National Greenhouse Gas Inventories, Volume 1, Chapter 8.5, https://www.ipcc-nggip.iges.or.jp/public/2006gl/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">CRF sector (IPCC 2006): electrical equipment</rdfs:label>
        <oeo:OEO_00010037>CRF 2.G.1</oeo:OEO_00010037>
        <oeo:OEO_00020426>issue: https://github.com/OpenEnergyPlatform/ontology/issues/1401
pull request: https://github.com/OpenEnergyPlatform/ontology/pull/1440

